@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false

left to right direction

title OpenStack - VXLAN entre compute1 y compute2 (datos reales)

cloud "RED DE GESTION (underlay)\n10.0.0.0/24\nTransporte VXLAN UDP 4789" as MGMT #E8F5E9
cloud "RED TENANT (overlay)\nselfservice-net 10.10.10.0/24" as TENANT #E3F2FD

frame "COMPUTE1\nHost: 203.0.113.240" as C1 {
  rectangle "IP br-mgmt: 10.0.0.10/24\nIP br-vxlan: 10.0.0.10/32" as C1IP #F5F5F5

  rectangle "br-int\nIntegration bridge\nConecta puertos tap + patch-tun" as C1INT #E1F5FE
  rectangle "br-tun\nTunnel bridge\nEncapsula/decapsula VXLAN" as C1TUN #EDE7F6
  rectangle "br-provider\nSalida provider (via br-vlan/enp8s0)" as C1PROV #E8F5E9

  rectangle "patch-tun" as C1P1 #FFFDE7
  rectangle "patch-int" as C1P2 #FFFDE7

  rectangle "VM en compute1\ntest-vm1 10.10.10.229\nEstado: SHUTOFF" as C1VM #FFEBEE
}

frame "COMPUTE2\nHost: 203.0.113.241" as C2 {
  rectangle "IP br-mgmt: 10.0.0.12/24\nIP br-vxlan: 10.0.0.12/32" as C2IP #F5F5F5

  rectangle "br-int\nIntegration bridge\nConecta puertos tap + patch-tun" as C2INT #E1F5FE
  rectangle "br-tun\nTunnel bridge\nEncapsula/decapsula VXLAN" as C2TUN #EDE7F6
  rectangle "br-provider\nSalida provider (via br-vlan/enp8s0)" as C2PROV #E8F5E9

  rectangle "patch-tun" as C2P1 #FFFDE7
  rectangle "patch-int" as C2P2 #FFFDE7

  rectangle "VMs WordPress en compute2\nwp-web-01 10.10.10.76 (FIP 192.168.122.137)\nwp-db-01 10.10.10.152 (FIP 192.168.122.152)" as C2VM #E8F5E9
}

C1INT --> C1P1
C1P1 --> C1TUN
C1TUN --> C1P2
C1P2 --> C1INT

C2INT --> C2P1
C2P1 --> C2TUN
C2TUN --> C2P2
C2P2 --> C2INT

C1INT -- C1VM : puertos tap (si VM activa)
C2INT -- C2VM : puertos tap activos

C1IP -- MGMT
C2IP -- MGMT

C1TUN <..> C2TUN : Tunel VXLAN\nUDP 4789\nLocal/Remote: 10.0.0.10 <-> 10.0.0.12

C1INT -- TENANT
C2INT -- TENANT

note bottom
Como leer este diagrama:
1) br-vxlan /32 NO es una red compartida; es identidad local del endpoint VXLAN.
2) El trafico VXLAN viaja por la red de gestion 10.0.0.0/24 (br-mgmt/enp7s0).
3) br-int integra puertos de VMs; br-tun encapsula/decapsula VXLAN; br-provider maneja salida provider.
4) En este estado, compute2 tiene VMs activas; compute1 tiene test-vm1 en SHUTOFF.
end note

@enduml
